% The customs background (lpsPlus docs/strategy/FactsBackground.md §6.1):
% how a marketplace listing speaks. Its fields, in the words of the tariff.
% Source: the description of the listings that are read
% (sources/listings/marketplace_fields.txt). Bridges.
%
% Used only to read facts from a listing (language reference §14.5); the
% tariff never reasons with it. The values of a noted fact are in lower case.

the target language is: prolog.

the functions are:
    the fabric construction of *a garment* is *a construction*.

the templates are:
    the field *a field* of *a thing* reads *a value*; undefined.
    *a value* is a gender value for *a gender*.
    *a value* is a construction value for *a construction*.
    *a thing* is called *a name*; undefined.
    *a thing* names the material *a name*; undefined.
    *a thing* names first the material *a name*; undefined.
    *a thing* is listed under the shop category *a category*; undefined.
    *a thing* is in the shop category *a category*.
    the cut of *a garment* indicates *a gender*.
    *a good* is a manufactured article.
    *a component* is a component of *a good*.
    *a value* is a sleeve value for sleeveless garments.
    *a field* is a field of the sleeves.
    *a garment* is sleeveless.

the knowledge base marketplace listings includes these resources:
    ../../../../lib/text.

the knowledge base marketplace listings includes:

the listing format is published at "https://huggingface.co/datasets/ATH-MaaS/HSCodeComp".
the text of the listing format is at "sources/listings/marketplace_fields.txt".
the other products listing format is published at "https://huggingface.co/datasets/ATH-MaaS/HSCodeComp".
the text of the other products listing format is at "sources/listings/marketplace_fields_other_products.txt".
the HTSUS Chapter 61 is published at "https://hts.usitc.gov/reststop/file?release=currentRelease&filename=Chapter%2061".
the text of the HTSUS Chapter 61 is at "sources/hts/chapter_61.txt".

"men" is a gender value for men,
    as stated in the listing format, confer "Gender: Men".
"women" is a gender value for women,
    as stated in the listing format, confer "Gender: Women".
"male" is a gender value for men,
    as stated in the listing format, confer "Gender (52 listings): for whom the product is made".
"female" is a gender value for women,
    as stated in the listing format, confer "Gender (52 listings): for whom the product is made".
"girls" is a gender value for women,
    as stated in the HTSUS Chapter 61, confer "Women's or girls' overcoats, carcoats, capes, cloaks, anoraks".
% Chapter 61 note 9 (and Chapter 62 note 8): a garment that is for neither
% sex alone goes to the women's headings
"unisex" is a gender value for women,
    as stated in the HTSUS Chapter 61, confer "Garments which cannot be identified as either men's or boys' garments or as women's or girls' garments are to be classified in".
"boys" is a gender value for men,
    as stated in the HTSUS Chapter 61, confer "Men's or boys' overcoats, carcoats, capes, cloaks, anoraks".

"knit" is a construction value for knitted,
    as stated in the listing format, confer "Craft of Weaving: Knit".
"non-woven" is a construction value for nonwoven,
    as stated in the listing format, confer "Craft of Weaving: Non-Woven".

% The sleeves: "sleeveless" is the tariff's word (Chapter 61 note 4,
% Chapter 62 note 4: "Heading 6105 does not cover sleeveless garments")
"sleeve length(cm)" is a field of the sleeves,
    as stated in the listing format, confer "Sleeve Length(cm) (26 listings), Sleeve Style (20 listings)".
"sleeve style" is a field of the sleeves,
    as stated in the listing format, confer "Sleeve Length(cm) (26 listings), Sleeve Style (20 listings)".
"sleeveless" is a sleeve value for sleeveless garments,
    as stated in the HTSUS Chapter 61, confer "Heading 6105 does not cover sleeveless garments".

rule finished_product with provenance the listing format,
        confer "A listing offers one finished product for sale":
a good is a manufactured article
    if the good is called a name.

rule finished_product_field with provenance the listing format,
        confer "A listing offers one finished product for sale":
a good is a manufactured article
    if the field a field of the good reads a value.

rule finished_product_material with provenance the listing format,
        confer "A listing offers one finished product for sale":
a good is a manufactured article
    if the good names the material a name.

rule gender_field with provenance the listing format,
        confer "Gender (52 listings): for whom the product is made":
the cut of a garment indicates a gender
    if the field "gender" of the garment reads a value
    and the value is a gender value for the gender.

rule sleeveless_field with provenance the HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "Heading 6105 does not cover sleeveless garments":
a garment is sleeveless
    if the field a field of the garment reads a value
    and the field is a field of the sleeves
    and the value is a sleeve value for sleeveless garments.

rule craft_of_weaving_field with provenance the listing format,
        confer "Craft of Weaving (54 listings): how the fabric is made":
the fabric construction of a garment is a construction
    if the field "craft of weaving" of the garment reads a value
    and the value is a construction value for the construction.

% A listing offers one product: a set's field on how the fabric is made
% speaks of each of its parts.
rule craft_of_weaving_field_parts with provenance the listing format,
        confer "A listing offers one finished product for sale":
the fabric construction of a component is a construction
    if the component is a component of a good
    and the field "craft of weaving" of the good reads a value
    and the value is a construction value for the construction.

rule materials_of_the_parts with provenance the listing format,
        confer "A listing offers one finished product for sale":
a component names the material a name
    if the component is a component of a good
    and the good names the material the name.

rule first_material_of_the_parts with provenance the listing format,
        confer "A listing offers one finished product for sale":
a component names first the material a name
    if the component is a component of a good
    and the good names first the material the name.

% The shop's category is a path of levels, the most general first ("Toys &
% Hobbies > Remote Control Toys"). The other backgrounds read each level.
rule category_levels with provenance the other products listing format,
        confer "The shop's first category is, for example:":
a thing is in the shop category a category
    if the thing is listed under the shop category a path
    and the path split at ">" has the part the category.

rule cut_of_the_parts with provenance the listing format,
        confer "A listing offers one finished product for sale":
the cut of a component indicates a gender
    if the component is a component of a good
    and the field "gender" of the good reads a value
    and the value is a gender value for the gender.

scenario knit_set is:
    the field "craft of weaving" of outfit reads "knit".
    outfit top is a component of outfit.
    outfit names first the material "polyester".
    the field "gender" of outfit reads "women".
    part_materials expects answers ["outfit names first the material polyester", "outfit top names first the material polyester"].
    part_cuts expects answers ["the cut of outfit indicates women", "the cut of outfit top indicates women"].
    set_constructions expects answers ["the fabric construction of outfit is knitted", "the fabric construction of outfit top is knitted"].

query part_materials is:
    which component names first the material which name.

query part_cuts is:
    the cut of which garment indicates which gender.

query set_constructions is:
    the fabric construction of which garment is which construction.

scenario tee is:
    the field "gender" of tee reads "men".
    the field "craft of weaving" of tee reads "knit".
    cuts expects answers ["the cut of tee indicates men"].
    constructions expects answers ["the fabric construction of tee is knitted"].
    articles expects answers ["tee is a manufactured article"].

scenario vest is:
    the field "sleeve length(cm)" of vest reads "sleeveless".
    the field "craft of weaving" of mask reads "non-woven".
    sleeves expects answers ["vest is sleeveless"].
    constructions expects answers ["the fabric construction of mask is nonwoven"].

query sleeves is:
    which garment is sleeveless.

query cuts is:
    the cut of which garment indicates which gender.

query constructions is:
    the fabric construction of which garment is which construction.

query articles is:
    which good is a manufactured article.

scenario category_levels is:
    item 1 is listed under the shop category "toys & hobbies > remote control toys".
    levels expects answers ["item 1 is in the shop category toys & hobbies", "item 1 is in the shop category remote control toys"].

query levels is:
    item 1 is in the shop category which category.
